{:edb/db-before-t 1579 :edb/db-after-t 1580 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534892 50 #inst "2026-10-08T10:17:06.191Z" 13194139534892 true] [17592186147366 1020 #edb/ref 17592186317918 13194139534892 true] [17592186147366 1020 #edb/ref 17592186317925 13194139534892 true] [17592186147366 1020 #edb/ref 17592186317946 13194139534892 true] [17592186147367 1020 #edb/ref 17592186317911 13194139534892 true] [17592186147367 1020 #edb/ref 17592186317939 13194139534892 true] [17592186147368 1020 #edb/ref 17592186317932 13194139534892 true] [17592186147368 1020 #edb/ref 17592186317953 13194139534892 true] [17592186148145 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534892 true] [17592186148145 1100 "Given the two planes $-x - 2y + z = 0$ and $2x + 4y - 2z + 1 = 0$, which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. The normal vectors of the planes are parallel.\n2. The planes are parallel but not coincident.\n3. The planes are coincident." 13194139534892 false] [17592186148145 1100 "Given the two planes $-x-2y+z=0$ and $2x+4y-2z+1=0$, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The normal vectors of the planes are parallel.\n- The planes are parallel but not coincident.\n- The planes are coincident." 13194139534892 true] [17592186148145 1145 "First, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $-x-2y+z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨-1,-2,1⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $2x+4y-2z+1=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨2,4,-2⟩.$\n\nNow, let's consider the statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, ${n}_{2}=-2{n}_{1}.$ So, the normal vectors are parallel.\n\n- Statement II is true, while statement III is false. \n\nFor the two planes to coincide, the equation of one plane should be a scalar multiple of the other. However, if we try to manipulate the equation of the second plane to resemble the equation of the first plane, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+4y-2z+1=0 \\\\ x+2y-z+\\frac{1}{2}=0 \\\\ -x-2y+z-\\frac{1}{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nClearly, this equation is not the same as the equation of the first plane. So, the planes are parallel but not coincident.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and II are true." 13194139534892 true] [17592186317911 1017 #edb/ref 17592186317912 13194139534892 true] [17592186317911 1089 "q-129169" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317911 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534892 true] [17592186317911 1100 "Find a direction vector of the line that is given as the intersection of the following two planes:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x+3z-11=0 \\\\ 2x-2y-5=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317911 1113 #uuid "d0aedac8-4550-5f55-b4ac-09ba9ac8ed13" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317911 1145 "First, we notice:\n\n- For the plane $2x+3z-11=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨2,0,3⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $2x-2y-5=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨2,-2,0⟩.$\n\nTo find a direction vector for the line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & ={n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} \\\\  & =⟨2,0,3⟩\\times ⟨2,-2,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =6i+6j-4k \\\\  & =⟨6,6,-4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317912 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317913 13194139534892 true] [17592186317912 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317914 13194139534892 true] [17592186317912 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317915 13194139534892 true] [17592186317912 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317916 13194139534892 true] [17592186317912 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317917 13194139534892 true] [17592186317912 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534892 true] [17592186317912 1041 "selection" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317912 1104 #edb/ref 17592186317915 13194139534892 true] [17592186317912 1110 #uuid "69826181-e839-534d-8f04-811418b3d660" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317913 1034 "⟨-4,6,6⟩" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317913 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534892 true] [17592186317913 1111 #uuid "787a7445-1cb7-5ac5-950f-51a380eb447f" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317914 1034 "⟨6,-4,6⟩" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317914 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534892 true] [17592186317914 1111 #uuid "c6c42555-612f-5d59-97c5-5290598a877c" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317915 1034 "⟨6,6,-4⟩" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317915 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534892 true] [17592186317915 1111 #uuid "44ddfb1d-f321-51e2-bdef-7bb63f8adccb" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317916 1034 "⟨4,-6,6⟩" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317916 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534892 true] [17592186317916 1111 #uuid "233189a9-7cc7-5e9b-803f-c63e072b07b7" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317917 1034 "⟨-6,4,-4⟩" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317917 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534892 true] [17592186317917 1111 #uuid "d7e54162-e89b-5dbb-ae32-c766417ba3b7" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317918 1017 #edb/ref 17592186317919 13194139534892 true] [17592186317918 1089 "q-129229" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317918 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534892 true] [17592186317918 1100 "The intersection of the planes $x+3y-2z-8=0$ and $2x+y-3z-16=0$ is given by the line\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨{a}_{1},0,{a}_{3}⟩+tb,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nCalculate ${a}_{1}+{a}_{3},$ and find a possible direction vector $b.$" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317918 1113 #uuid "5d143e7a-cebc-5440-b9bb-3b483458d2cf" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317918 1145 "We're given that there exists a point on the line where $y=0.$ Substituting this into the second equation gives \n\n$$\nx+0-2z-8=0\\,⟹\\,x=2z+8,\n$$\n\nand substituting $y=0$ and $x=2z+8$ into the first equation gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(2z+8)+0-3z-16 & =0 \\\\ 4z+16-3z-16 & =0 \\\\ z & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $x=2(0)+8=8$ and $a=⟨8,0,0⟩$ is a position vector of a point on the line.\n\nNext, we notice:\n\n- For the plane $x+3y-2z-8=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨1,3,-2⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $2x+y-3z-16=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨2,1,-3⟩.$\n\nTo find a direction vector for the line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨1,3,-2⟩\\times ⟨2,1,-3⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-7i-j-5k \\\\  & =⟨-7,-1,-5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the equation of the line is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =a+tb \\\\ r(t) & =⟨8,0,0⟩+t⟨-7,-1,-5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally then, ${a}_{1}+{a}_{3}=8+0=8,$ and $b=⟨-7,-1,-5⟩.$" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317919 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317920 13194139534892 true] [17592186317919 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317921 13194139534892 true] [17592186317919 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317922 13194139534892 true] [17592186317919 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317923 13194139534892 true] [17592186317919 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317924 13194139534892 true] [17592186317919 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534892 true] [17592186317919 1041 "selection" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317919 1104 #edb/ref 17592186317922 13194139534892 true] [17592186317919 1110 #uuid "891db865-96ab-540e-b237-c18f5e352742" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317920 1034 "{a}_{1}+{a}_{3}=4,\\,b=⟨-1,-7,5⟩" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317920 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534892 true] [17592186317920 1111 #uuid "792797aa-dac9-5b13-8d48-232f5a08494b" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317921 1034 "{a}_{1}+{a}_{3}=-8,\\,b=⟨-7,5,-1⟩" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317921 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534892 true] [17592186317921 1111 #uuid "ffc03c30-6c94-5d79-9ea3-0d3bab7e87e2" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317922 1034 "{a}_{1}+{a}_{3}=8,\\,b=⟨-7,-1,-5⟩" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317922 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534892 true] [17592186317922 1111 #uuid "aad9b1ce-b023-529c-9ca6-2465308721f7" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317923 1034 "{a}_{1}+{a}_{3}=-4,\\,b=⟨-5,-1,7⟩" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317923 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534892 true] [17592186317923 1111 #uuid "1eb79c25-6570-5656-8f4b-0aa89eb79556" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317924 1034 "{a}_{1}+{a}_{3}=7,\\,b=⟨-8,-5,1⟩" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317924 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534892 true] [17592186317924 1111 #uuid "c9d9707f-bbe3-5514-b6c7-4435b3b448b0" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317925 1017 #edb/ref 17592186317926 13194139534892 true] [17592186317925 1089 "q-129238" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317925 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534892 true] [17592186317925 1100 "The intersection of the planes $x+y-z-3=0$ and $x+2y-3z+18=0$ is given by the line\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨{a}_{1},{a}_{2},0⟩+tb,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nCalculate ${a}_{1}+{a}_{2},$ and find a possible direction vector $b.$" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317925 1113 #uuid "d6407551-67a9-560e-b723-72e719f9cb5c" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317925 1145 "We're given that there exists a point on the line where $z=0.$ Substituting this into the first equation gives  \n\n$$\nx+y-0-3=0\\,⟹\\,x=3-y,\n$$\n\nand substituting $z=0$ and $x=3-y$ into the second equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3-y)+2y-3(0)+18 & =0 \\\\ 3+y+18 & =0 \\\\ y & =-21.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $x=3-y=3+21=24$ and $a=⟨24,-21,0⟩$ is a position vector of a point on the line.\n\nNext, we notice:\n\n- For the plane $x+y-z-3=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨1,1,-1⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $x+2y-3z+18=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨1,2,-3⟩.$\n\nTo find a direction vector for the line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨1,1,-1⟩\\times ⟨1,2,-3⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -3\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-i+2j+k \\\\  & =⟨-1,2,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the equation of the line is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =a+tb \\\\ r(t) & =⟨24,-21,0⟩+t⟨-1,2,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally then, ${a}_{1}+{a}_{2}=24-21=3,$ and $b=⟨-1,2,1⟩.$" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317926 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317927 13194139534892 true] [17592186317926 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317928 13194139534892 true] [17592186317926 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317929 13194139534892 true] [17592186317926 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317930 13194139534892 true] [17592186317926 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317931 13194139534892 true] [17592186317926 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534892 true] [17592186317926 1041 "selection" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317926 1104 #edb/ref 17592186317927 13194139534892 true] [17592186317926 1110 #uuid "b1d2c490-607d-5fd2-bf7b-1eb2ec0dceb3" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317927 1034 "{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}=3,\\,b=⟨-1,2,1⟩" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317927 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534892 true] [17592186317927 1111 #uuid "2255437b-2a7c-5d4b-ad0d-c5342e87f421" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317928 1034 "{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}=6,\\,b=⟨-2,1,1⟩" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317928 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534892 true] [17592186317928 1111 #uuid "6a9ec6e5-63a1-5ba1-aca6-2d683cb7adfb" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317929 1034 "{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}=5,\\,b=⟨1,2,1⟩" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317929 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534892 true] [17592186317929 1111 #uuid "b2667c7c-92a3-53f3-b37b-df98b05ec599" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317930 1034 "{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}=-6,\\,b=⟨-2,1,-1⟩" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317930 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534892 true] [17592186317930 1111 #uuid "df20b430-25c3-5035-a27e-d4983f0fe92a" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317931 1034 "{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}=-3,\\,b=⟨-1,1,2⟩" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317931 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534892 true] [17592186317931 1111 #uuid "1997b8a8-bf75-5ad1-9f36-d3435660bf7b" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317932 1017 #edb/ref 17592186317933 13194139534892 true] [17592186317932 1089 "q-129261" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317932 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534892 true] [17592186317932 1100 "Given the two planes $x-y+2z=0$ and $5x+y-13=0$, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $⟨-3,12,6⟩.$\n- The planes intersect on a line.\n- The planes are coincident." 13194139534892 true] [17592186317932 1113 #uuid "22e39499-5747-5698-af95-b4fc0c4d8191" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317932 1145 "First, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $x-y+2z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨1,-1,2⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $5x+y-13=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨5,1,0⟩.$\n\nNow, let's consider the statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed, computing the cross product of the normal vectors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨1,-1,2⟩\\times ⟨5,1,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-2i+10j+6k \\\\  & =⟨-2,10,6⟩\\ne ⟨-3,12,6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Since ${n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2}\\ne 0$, the vectors ${n}_{1}$ and ${n}_{2}$ are not parallel. Hence, the corresponding planes must intersect on a line.\n\n- Statement III is false. Indeed, two non-parallel planes could not be coincident either.\n\nTherefore, only statement II is true." 13194139534892 true] [17592186317933 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317934 13194139534892 true] [17592186317933 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317935 13194139534892 true] [17592186317933 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317936 13194139534892 true] [17592186317933 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317937 13194139534892 true] [17592186317933 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317938 13194139534892 true] [17592186317933 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534892 true] [17592186317933 1041 "selection" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317933 1104 #edb/ref 17592186317938 13194139534892 true] [17592186317933 1110 #uuid "7ddbfadd-a8b1-5f1f-ad22-809f6ba2beaa" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317934 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317934 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534892 true] [17592186317934 1111 #uuid "bac37965-8c39-5fe8-8477-dca2f06947a0" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317935 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317935 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534892 true] [17592186317935 1111 #uuid "f3baef66-cb25-55f8-9dcb-524cc89acc3f" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317936 1034 "III only" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317936 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534892 true] [17592186317936 1111 #uuid "4967c162-3d17-5ddc-89c4-29461e0fb076" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317937 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317937 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534892 true] [17592186317937 1111 #uuid "434a6c0a-9995-57aa-ae40-2f5688e38d1f" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317938 1034 "II only" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317938 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534892 true] [17592186317938 1111 #uuid "d0910555-34fd-5736-bb97-1bfe04b7cec3" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317939 1017 #edb/ref 17592186317940 13194139534892 true] [17592186317939 1089 "q-71269" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317939 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534892 true] [17592186317939 1100 "Find a direction vector of the line that is given as the intersection of the planes $x=1$ and $y=-z.$" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317939 1113 #uuid "cd7b78c1-6586-5772-840d-06dfdf6ee176" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317939 1145 "First, notice that: \n\n- For the plane $x=1$, a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨1,0,0⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $y=-z$ (or $y+z=0$), a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨0,1,1⟩.$\n\nTo find a direction vector for the line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & ={n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} \\\\  & =⟨1,0,0⟩\\times ⟨0,1,1⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-j+k \\\\  & =⟨0,-1,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317940 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317941 13194139534892 true] [17592186317940 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317942 13194139534892 true] [17592186317940 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317943 13194139534892 true] [17592186317940 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317944 13194139534892 true] [17592186317940 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317945 13194139534892 true] [17592186317940 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534892 true] [17592186317940 1041 "selection" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317940 1104 #edb/ref 17592186317943 13194139534892 true] [17592186317940 1110 #uuid "b744509a-aaf3-5773-a166-8fa33cb468e4" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317941 1034 "⟨1,1,-1⟩" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317941 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534892 true] [17592186317941 1111 #uuid "8f532964-059a-56c1-8751-a27bf1f4829e" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317942 1034 "⟨0,-1,-1⟩" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317942 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534892 true] [17592186317942 1111 #uuid "87d707d9-d5f1-53ed-a5e1-0f9e11a83245" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317943 1034 "⟨0,-1,1⟩" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317943 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534892 true] [17592186317943 1111 #uuid "34a73aaa-8712-5c38-ba6a-d74ec3011a05" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317944 1034 "⟨0,1,1⟩" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317944 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534892 true] [17592186317944 1111 #uuid "eb89f0ce-7a3f-5319-a7ee-579a4fbb60eb" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317945 1034 "⟨1,1,1⟩" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317945 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534892 true] [17592186317945 1111 #uuid "708b3e8a-7f69-5439-a602-c231abac9e14" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317946 1017 #edb/ref 17592186317947 13194139534892 true] [17592186317946 1089 "q-71446" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317946 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534892 true] [17592186317946 1100 "The intersection of the planes $x+2y+3z=0$ and $3x+2y+z+8=0$ is given by the line\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨{a}_{1},0,{a}_{3}⟩+tb,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nCalculate ${a}_{1}+{a}_{3},$ and find a possible direction vector $b.$" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317946 1113 #uuid "61cf4d39-9683-533e-9394-f4988b6cbe81" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317946 1145 "We're given that there exists a point on the line where $y=0.$ Substituting this into the first equation gives    \n\n$$\nx+2(0)+3z=0\\,⟹\\,x=-3z,\n$$\n\nand substituting $y=0$ and $x=-3z$ into the second equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+2y+z+8 & =0 \\\\ 3(-3z)+2(0)+z+8 & =0 \\\\ -8z & =-8 \\\\ z & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $x=-3z=-3$ and $a=⟨-3,0,1⟩$ is a position vector of a point on the line.\n\nNext, we notice:\n\n- For the plane $x+2y+3z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨1,2,3⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $3x+2y+z+8=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨3,2,1⟩.$\n\nTo find a direction vector for the line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨1,2,3⟩\\times ⟨3,2,1⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-4i+8j-4k \\\\  & =⟨-4,8,-4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can pick any vector that is parallel to ${n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2}$ as a direction vector of the line. So, let \n\n$$\nb=-\\frac{1}{4}({n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2})=⟨1,-2,1⟩.\n$$\n\nThe equation of the line is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =a+tb \\\\ r(t) & =⟨-3,0,1⟩+t⟨1,-2,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally then, ${a}_{1}+{a}_{3}=-3+1=-2,$ and $b=⟨1,-2,1⟩.$" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317947 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317948 13194139534892 true] [17592186317947 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317949 13194139534892 true] [17592186317947 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317950 13194139534892 true] [17592186317947 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317951 13194139534892 true] [17592186317947 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317952 13194139534892 true] [17592186317947 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534892 true] [17592186317947 1041 "selection" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317947 1104 #edb/ref 17592186317948 13194139534892 true] [17592186317947 1110 #uuid "dddf3ab9-17c6-51d5-a9ad-06d3404c0068" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317948 1034 "{a}_{1}+{a}_{3}=-2,\\,b=⟨1,-2,1⟩" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317948 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534892 true] [17592186317948 1111 #uuid "fd8ed127-be85-544a-bc03-1806ffa03548" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317949 1034 "{a}_{1}+{a}_{3}=-3,\\,b=⟨1,-2,3⟩" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317949 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534892 true] [17592186317949 1111 #uuid "ada6b8f6-5526-5e24-ad84-0b05b1181052" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317950 1034 "{a}_{1}+{a}_{3}=3,\\,b=⟨-1,-2,-3⟩" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317950 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534892 true] [17592186317950 1111 #uuid "bce644e9-3d29-5fa1-af4d-33771a072e5e" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317951 1034 "{a}_{1}+{a}_{3}=2,\\,b=⟨2,-2,3⟩" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317951 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534892 true] [17592186317951 1111 #uuid "e881c0c4-9a27-5d88-9335-7ba7bebb29d5" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317952 1034 "{a}_{1}+{a}_{3}=2,\\,b=⟨1,2,1⟩" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317952 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534892 true] [17592186317952 1111 #uuid "2e11eee1-0155-5d84-96b6-03d1ea939615" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317953 1017 #edb/ref 17592186317954 13194139534892 true] [17592186317953 1089 "q-71463" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317953 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534892 true] [17592186317953 1100 "Given the two planes $3x+3y+2z=0$ and $x-y-z=0$, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $⟨1,6,-5⟩.$\n- The planes are parallel.\n- The planes intersect on a line." 13194139534892 true] [17592186317953 1113 #uuid "c0212fc2-f78c-514d-ac95-d9fd26dc0ceb" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317953 1145 "First, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $3x+3y+2z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨3,3,2⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $x-y-z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨1,-1,-1⟩.$\n\nNow, let's consider the statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. Computing the cross product of the normal vectors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨3,3,2⟩\\times ⟨1,-1,-1⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-i+5j-6k \\\\  & =⟨-1,5,-6⟩\\ne ⟨1,6,-5⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since ${n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2}\\ne 0$, the vectors ${n}_{1}$ and ${n}_{2}$ are not parallel. As a result, the corresponding planes are not parallel either.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, two non-parallel planes in $3$-dimensional space must intersect on a line.\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true." 13194139534892 true] [17592186317954 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317955 13194139534892 true] [17592186317954 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317956 13194139534892 true] [17592186317954 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317957 13194139534892 true] [17592186317954 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317958 13194139534892 true] [17592186317954 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317959 13194139534892 true] [17592186317954 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534892 true] [17592186317954 1041 "selection" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317954 1104 #edb/ref 17592186317958 13194139534892 true] [17592186317954 1110 #uuid "db363893-de21-563c-b1a8-bb84a9a85da9" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317955 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317955 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534892 true] [17592186317955 1111 #uuid "308325ff-1cef-5051-a5e8-80a4f61c1912" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317956 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317956 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534892 true] [17592186317956 1111 #uuid "9b4a1fc4-4222-51fe-b3da-0ee4c2222007" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317957 1034 "I only" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317957 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534892 true] [17592186317957 1111 #uuid "5c3bf136-3ab6-5529-91cb-fe72aa416075" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317958 1034 "III only" 13194139534892 true] [17592186317958 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534892 true] [17592186317958 1111 #uuid "05509d3f-017b-515f-81bf-22b6415a40b7" 13194139534892 true